{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VimTWg2cuLovcARyVUi25g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the task carefully:\n\n1. I need to create `cmd/sponge/sponge_test.go` - a differential test file for the sponge utility\n2. I need to follow the pattern from `cmd/cat/cat_test.go` \n3. I need to use `pkg/testutils` for differential testing\n4. The reference binary is `sponge` (not `gsponge` - moreutils doesn't use g- prefix)\n\nLet me review the requirements:\n- R1: Test stdin soaking before writing to output file (ExpectedFiles)\n- R2: Test atomic write to named output file (ExpectedFiles, exit code 0)\n\n\n- R3: Test -a append mode (pre-existing content + stdin via ExpectedFiles)\n- R4: Test passthrough mode (no file arg, stdout matches stdin)\n\nI'll set up TestMain to build the Go sponge binary and locate the reference binary via LookPath, skipping if not found, then structure each test case with a temporary directory and a helper function for writing test files.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35221,"cache_read_input_tokens":16066,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35221},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fad0d12d-b0ad-4247-8519-7c41385bf7d6","uuid":"46d989d9-cd0e-41a8-a139-20c64f50c401"}
